pecially in Asia. The internodes of bamboos can also be of great length. Kinabaluchloa wrayi has internodes up to 2.5 meters (8 ft) in length, and Arthrostylidium schomburgkii has internodes up to 5 meters (16 ft) in length, exceeded in length only by papyrus.  By contrast, the stalks of the tiny bamboo Raddiella vanessiae of the savannas of French Guiana measure only 10–20 millimeters (0.4–0.8 in) in length by about 2 millimeters (0.08 in) in widt"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bamboo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Lemang","dish/lemang"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Glutinous rice","ingredient/glutinous-rice"]]}]},"dish/moules-frites":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/moules-frites","n":"Moules-frites","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Belgian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Moules-frites or moules et frites is a main dish of mussels and French fries originating in Northern France and Belgium. The name is French, moules meaning mussels and frites fries, with the Dutch name for the dish meaning the same. It is the national dish of Belgium."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-moules-frites"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moules-frites"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Blue mussel","ingredient/blue-mussel"],["Fries","ingredient/fries"]]},{"h":"More from Belgian cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["Algérienne sauce","dish/algerienne-sauce"],["Belgian chocolate","dish/belgian-chocolate"],["Belgo","dish/belgo"],["Bickyburger","dish/bickyburger"],["Boûkète","dish/boukete"],["Flemish stew","dish/flemish-stew"],["Friteri